atemala","url":"https://www.wanderlustmagazine.com/inspiration/maya-food-guatemala/"},{"name":"México Desconocido, Ruta de cocineras tradicionales, de Santa Fe de la Laguna a Tarecuato","url":"https://www.mexicodesconocido.com.mx/ruta-de-cocineras-tradicionales-de-santa-fe-de-la-laguna-tarecuato.html"},{"name":"University of Texas at Austin, Tlahtolli, Our cornfield and our food","url":"https://tlahtolli.coerll.utexas.edu/tlamachtiliztli-20-lesson-20-nomillah-huah-notlacualiztli-our-cornfield-and-our-food/"},{"name":"Warasa Garifuna Drum School, Garifuna food","url":"https://www.warasadrumschool.com/garifuna-culture/garifuna-food"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tamale"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamale"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Latin American cuisine","cuisine/latin-american-cuisine"],["Maya cuisine","cuisine/maya-cuisine"],["Purépecha foodways","cuisine/purepecha-foodways"],["Nahua foodways","cuisine/nahua-foodways"],["Garifuna foodways","cuisine/garifuna-foodways"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":8,"links":[["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Corn husks","ingredient/corn-husks"],["Cornmeal","ingredient/cornmeal"],["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Masa","ingredient/masa"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Nahua Siwameh itech Tlekuille","ref":"site/artsandculture-google-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"artsandculture.google.com","note":"Recipes and photos from Nahua women cooks of the Sierra de Zongolica, Veracruz.","url":"https://artsandculture.google.com/story/JgWhWhzqlzrcMQ","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Latin American cuisine","links":[["Bollo","dish/bollo"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Cardenas (supermarket)","dish/cardenas-supermarket"],["El Cielo (restaurant)","dish/el-cielo-restaurant"],["Frijoles negros","dish/frijoles-negros"],["La Michoacana Meat Market","dish/la-michoacana-meat-market"],["Mi Pueblo Food Center","dish/mi-pueblo-food-center"],["Quince cheese","dish/quince-cheese"],["Rice and beans","dish/rice-and-beans"],["Vallarta Supermarkets","dish/vallarta-supermarkets"]]}]},"dish/tumpeng":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tumpeng","n":"Tumpeng","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tumpeng is an Indonesian cone-shaped rice dish with side dishes of vegetables and meat originating from Javanese cuisine. Traditionally featured in the slametan ceremony, the rice is made by using a cone-shaped woven bamboo container. As its counterpart the Spanish paella, today it can be found in other celebrations as well, such as for birthdays or parties. The rice itself may be plain steamed rice, uduk rice (cooked with coconut milk), or yellow rice (uduk rice colored with turmeric)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tumpeng"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumpeng"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Anchovy","ingredient/anchovy"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Fried chicken","ingredient/fried-chicken"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Tempeh","ingredient/tempeh"],["Urab","ingredient/urab"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hay